{
  "meta": {
    "version": 3,
    "updatedBy": "copilot",
    "note": "Windows Fluent UI for OpenClaw — ported from the v1 raw-CSS components.jsonc to v3 Auto Layout. WinUI-derived pixel padding is snapped to the nearest 4px spacing token; per-component notes record the source values and any approximation. Chat components track the native chat refresh in docs/CHAT_VISUAL_DESIGN.md and Themes/ChatResources.xaml (#1459): message and code surfaces use the `bubble` (12px) radius, the composer uses the `composer` (20px) radius, and chat binds the chat-local ChatResources brushes. Workspace-shell components (AgentIdentityBadge, ConnectionStatusFlyout, NotificationFlyout, WorkspaceShell) mirror the native Home and Sessions workspace shipped in #1541: WorkspaceWindow.xaml (Mica shell, left NavigationView, Owner footer), Controls/AgentIdentityBadge.xaml, Controls/GatewayStatusContent.xaml, and Controls/NotificationFlyoutContent.xaml are the source of truth; token bindings follow their ThemeResource keys."
  },
  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Button",
      "note": "Basic control. Primary action — one per view, where the eye should land. Previewed as `variant:primary`, the WinUI AccentButtonStyle: `accent` fill (AccentFillColorDefaultBrush) with `accentInk` text (TextOnAccentFillColorPrimaryBrush), `sm` radius (ControlCornerRadius). Hover = AccentFillColorSecondary (token `accentSubtle`); pressed = AccentFillColorTertiary (no exact token, previewed with `accentSubtle`, documented here); disabled = AccentFillColorDisabled with TextOnAccentFillColorDisabled (previewed as `control`/`muted`). The `variant:standard` Button swaps to the default ButtonStyle: `control` fill (ControlFillColorDefault), `controlLine` border (ControlStrokeColorDefault), `ink` text; hover ControlFillColorSecondary, pressed ControlFillColorTertiary, disabled ControlFillColorDisabled. Subtle/icon buttons are the separate SubtleButton block. Padding mirrors WinUI ButtonPadding (11,5,11,6), snapped to spacing tokens 3 (12≈11) and 1 (4≈5/6). In-app MinWidth 100px keeps short labels (OK / Connect) from cramping and gives side-by-side buttons a consistent footprint; that minimum has no spacing-token equivalent, so it stays a port note and the preview hugs its label.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Save changes",
        "variant": "primary"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "class": "ds-btn ds-btn-{variant}",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "padding": {
            "x": "3",
            "y": "1"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "accentInk",
          "background": "accent",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "pressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "control" }
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Field",
      "note": "Basic control. Text input with a quiet label above it — the field is the subject. The input ships as the default WinUI TextBox: `control` fill (ControlFillColorDefault), `controlLine` hairline border (ControlStrokeColorDefault), `ink` text, `sm` radius. Hover = ControlFillColorSecondary (no exact token; previewed with `control`, documented here). Focus draws the Fluent accent underline, previewed as a `accent` bottom border via `states.focus`. Disabled = ControlFillColorDisabled with `muted` text. Input padding mirrors WinUI TextControlThemePadding (10,5,6,6), snapped to tokens 2 (8≈10/6 horizontal) and 1 (4≈5/6 vertical). In-app MinHeight 32px lines a field up with a Button on the same row; that minimum stays a port note. Focus draws the Fluent accent underline, supplied here by `control.focus` (accent rectangle); the OFF-grid hover tint (ControlFillColorSecondary) has no exact token and previews with `control`.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Gateway address",
        "placeholder": "127.0.0.1:18789"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "field-root",
        "el": "label",
        "class": "ds-field",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "vertical",
          "gap": "2",
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "field-label",
            "el": "span",
            "class": "ds-field-label",
            "children": [
              "{label}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "field-input",
            "el": "input",
            "class": "ds-input",
            "attrs": {
              "placeholder": "{placeholder}"
            },
            "layout": {
              "padding": {
                "x": "2",
                "y": "1"
              },
              "width": "fill"
            },
            "appearance": {
              "fontFamily": "body",
              "textStyle": "body",
              "color": "ink",
              "background": "control",
              "borderColor": "controlLine",
              "radius": "sm"
            },
            "control": {
              "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
            },
            "states": {
              "hover": { "background": "control" },
              "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "control" }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Card",
      "note": "Content card. Flat by default — a 1px hairline border, not a drop shadow. Padding mirrors the WinUI Gallery card (16,12) as tokens 4 (16) and 3 (12) exactly, with the `md` radius and a `line`-colored border supplied by the ds-card class. Never nest a card inside a card.",
      "props": {
        "title": "Windows node",
        "body": "Paired · 6 capabilities exposed over MCP."
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "card-root",
        "el": "article",
        "class": "ds-card",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "vertical",
          "gap": "2",
          "padding": {
            "x": "4",
            "y": "3"
          },
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "card-title",
            "el": "h3",
            "class": "ds-card-title",
            "children": [
              "{title}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "card-body",
            "el": "p",
            "class": "ds-card-body",
            "children": [
              "{body}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "card-link",
            "el": "a",
            "class": "ds-link",
            "attrs": {
              "href": "#"
            },
            "margin": {
              "top": "1"
            },
            "children": [
              "Open report →"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Badge",
      "note": "Basic control. Status pill — a read-only, non-interactive label, so it carries no hover/pressed states. Uses semantic color tokens, never a raw hex: `positive` (SystemFillColorSuccess), `warning` (SystemFillColorCaution), `critical` (SystemFillColorCritical), or `muted` for neutral. Padding tokens 3/1 give the pill a compact footprint; the `pill` radius and tone color come from the ds-badge class. Two production relatives: the WorkspaceShell count badge is a Fluent InfoBadge (default pill geometry, framework fill), and the notification recurrence badge is a 10px-radius `warning` subtle-background chip with 7,1 padding — both non-interactive, documented on their host components.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Connected",
        "tone": "positive"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "badge-root",
        "el": "span",
        "class": "ds-badge ds-badge-{tone}",
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "padding": {
            "x": "3",
            "y": "1"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "SubtleButton",
      "note": "Basic control. The quiet icon button used across the workspace chrome and flyouts (WinUI SubtleButtonStyle): Back/Forward, New session, pane toggle, notification bell, and the flyout dismiss button. Transparent rest (SubtleFillColorTransparent, `$none`) with a glyph in `ink`; hover = SubtleFillColorSecondary (`subtleHover`), pressed = SubtleFillColorTertiary (`subtlePressed`), disabled = ControlFillColorDisabled with `muted` glyph. `sm` radius (ControlCornerRadius). Previewed at the workspace command size 40x40 with a 16px glyph (WorkspaceWindow.xaml uses Width/Height 40, FontSize 16); the notification dismiss variant is 30x30 with an 11px glyph and 6px padding. `control.chrome:none` removes the web button border so the transparent Windows rest state shows, and `control.focus` draws the accent focus rectangle. Glyph shown is New session (Segoe Fluent Add, U+E710).",
      "props": {
        "label": "New session"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "subtle-button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "width": 40,
          "height": 40
        },
        "appearance": {
          "color": "ink",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "subtleHover" },
          "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "$none" }
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "subtle-button-glyph",
            "el": "span",
            "attrs": {
              "aria-hidden": "true",
              "style": "font-family:'Segoe Fluent Icons','Segoe MDL2 Assets',sans-serif;font-size:16px"
            },
            "children": [
              "\uE710"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "HyperlinkButton",
      "note": "Basic control. WinUI HyperlinkButton used for inline navigation and quiet actions (Reconnect, Approve, Open Connection, Clear all, Open notifications). Accent link text (system accent hyperlink brush, token `accent`) with no border or fill at rest; hover shows the subtle wash (SubtleFillColorSecondary, `subtleHover`) and pressed deepens to SubtleFillColorTertiary (`subtlePressed`); disabled drops to `muted`. Horizontal padding mirrors the production `Padding=4,0` (token `1` left/right, no vertical pad); `sm` radius. Text uses the `body` scale. `control.chrome:none` strips the web button chrome; `control.focus` supplies the accent focus rectangle.",
      "props": {
        "children": "Open Connection"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "hyperlink-button-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "padding": {
            "left": "1",
            "right": "1"
          },
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "body",
          "color": "accent",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "subtleHover" },
          "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "$none" }
        },
        "children": [
          "{children}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ToggleSwitch",
      "note": "Basic control. The stock WinUI ToggleSwitch used on settings and permission rows. Previewed in the ON state: track fills `accent` (AccentFillColorDefault / ToggleSwitchFillOn) with an `accentInk` (TextOnAccentFillColorPrimary) thumb pushed right. OFF state (documented as a port note): track is `control` (ControlFillColorDefault) with a `controlLine` border and a `muted`/ControlStrongFill thumb at left. Hover = AccentFillColorSecondary on (ControlFillColorSecondary off); pressed = AccentFillColorTertiary on (ControlFillColorTertiary off); disabled uses the Fluent disabled track. Track previewed at 40x20 with a `pill` radius and a 14px circular thumb; the thumb/track visuals are WinUI template parts and are a port note. Toggle-state brushes are stock Fluent resources, not locally remapped.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Launch at startup"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "toggle-switch-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button",
          "role": "switch",
          "aria-checked": "true",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "end",
          "padding": { "x": "1" },
          "width": 40,
          "height": 20
        },
        "appearance": {
          "background": "accent",
          "radius": "pill"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "pressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "accentSubtle" },
          "disabled": { "background": "control" }
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "toggle-switch-thumb",
            "el": "span",
            "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" },
            "layout": { "width": 14, "height": 14 },
            "appearance": { "background": "accentInk", "radius": "pill" }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "StatusDot",
      "note": "Basic control. The 10x10 connection/status indicator reused in the gateway flyout (Ellipse), the workspace Owner footer (10px FontIcon), and the identity badges. Non-interactive, so no hover/pressed states. Fill is a semantic token; previewed `positive` (SystemFillColorSuccess) for connected, and the variants are `warning` (SystemFillColorCaution) attention, `critical` (SystemFillColorCritical) error, and `muted`/neutral unknown. 10px sits between spacing tokens (nearest `2`=8); previewed at a literal 10x10 with a `pill` radius.",
      "props": {
        "tone": "positive"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "status-dot-root",
        "el": "span",
        "attrs": {
          "role": "img",
          "aria-label": "Connected"
        },
        "layout": {
          "width": 10,
          "height": 10
        },
        "appearance": {
          "background": "positive",
          "radius": "pill"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Avatar",
      "note": "Basic control. WinUI PersonPicture circular avatar. Non-interactive. The agent avatar is 32x32 (AgentIdentityBadge), the workspace Owner avatar is 24x24; both render a circular initials/photo tile. Previewed at 32x32 with a `pill` radius and a `muted` placeholder fill plus `ink`-on-muted initials; real photo/initials and the circular clip are WinUI template behavior and a port note.",
      "props": {
        "initials": "AU"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "avatar-root",
        "el": "span",
        "attrs": {
          "role": "img"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "align": "center",
          "justify": "center",
          "width": 32,
          "height": 32
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "small",
          "color": "ink",
          "background": "muted",
          "radius": "pill"
        },
        "children": [
          "{initials}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "InfoBar",
      "note": "Basic control. The Fluent InfoBar severity banner used for workspace operation errors and app notifications (WorkspaceWindow OperationInfo, HubWindow AppNotificationInfoBar, ChatPage). Previewed at Error severity: a `surface` sheet with a `line` hairline, `md` radius, and 16px padding, led by a `critical` status glyph (Segoe Fluent Error, U+EA39), a `ink` BodyStrong title, a `muted` caption message, and a trailing SubtleButton close (U+E711). Severity recolors the leading glyph only: `critical` Error, `warning` Warning, `positive` Success, `accent` Informational. The banner body is non-interactive; the close button carries the shared subtle hover/pressed states.",
      "props": {
        "title": "Couldn't reach the gateway",
        "message": "Check that the gateway is running, then retry."
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "info-bar-root",
        "el": "div",
        "attrs": { "role": "status" },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "gap": "3",
          "padding": "4",
          "align": "start",
          "width": "fill"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "background": "surface",
          "borderColor": "line",
          "radius": "md"
        },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "info-bar-icon",
            "el": "span",
            "attrs": {
              "aria-hidden": "true",
              "style": "font-family:'Segoe Fluent Icons','Segoe MDL2 Assets',sans-serif;font-size:16px"
            },
            "appearance": { "color": "critical" },
            "children": [ "\uEA39" ]
          },
          {
            "id": "info-bar-text",
            "el": "div",
            "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "1", "grow": true, "width": "fill" },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "info-bar-title",
                "el": "span",
                "appearance": { "fontFamily": "body", "textStyle": "body", "color": "ink" },
                "children": [ "{title}" ]
              },
              {
                "id": "info-bar-message",
                "el": "span",
                "appearance": { "fontFamily": "body", "textStyle": "caption", "color": "muted" },
                "children": [ "{message}" ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "info-bar-close",
            "el": "button",
            "attrs": { "type": "button", "aria-label": "Close" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "align": "center", "justify": "center", "width": 30, "height": 30 },
            "appearance": { "color": "muted", "background": "$none", "radius": "sm" },
            "control": {
              "chrome": "none",
              "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
            },
            "states": {
              "hover": { "background": "subtleHover" },
              "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
              "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" }
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "info-bar-close-glyph",
                "el": "span",
                "attrs": {
                  "aria-hidden": "true",
                  "style": "font-family:'Segoe Fluent Icons','Segoe MDL2 Assets',sans-serif;font-size:11px"
                },
                "children": [ "\uE711" ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPicker",
      "note": "Subtle inline dropdown. Ships as a WinUI subtle DropDownButton (a transparent Button that opens a flyout), NOT a bordered ComboBox and NOT a Fluent-web pill/segmented control. Shows the current value in `muted` secondary text (TextFillColorSecondary) with a trailing `muted` chevron (Segoe Fluent \\uE70D, previewed ~10px). 32px min height; horizontal padding token `2`, gap token `1`; `sm` radius = WinUI ControlCornerRadius (4px). It is a real `button` whose browser chrome is removed with `control.chrome:none`, so the transparent WinUI rest state (SubtleFillColorTransparent, `$none`) shows with no web button border, and `control.focus` supplies the Windows accent focus rectangle instead of a web focus ring. Hover uses `subtleHover` (SubtleFillColorSecondary) and press uses `subtlePressed` (SubtleFillColorTertiary) through `states`, so the picker stays quiet in the composer toolbar and never competes with the primary Send action. When there is nothing to choose (for example the session picker with a single session) the picker is disabled and its value reads a shade lighter than the enabled muted text. Used for the model, reasoning-effort, and session selectors; `on.click` opens the picker flyout. Since #1459 the model picker is a native flyout with an AutoSuggestBox over a grouped, single-selection ListView, and the reasoning-effort picker is a native discrete slider with a compact gauge trigger (`ChatEffortGauge`, rendered with WinUI paths, not a font glyph) at narrow widths; a picker trigger value can tint with `ChatPickerAccentBrush`. The session selector stays a single-select flyout. ComposerPickerOptions is a representative shared option list because flyout targets take no props; the real per-picker option sets (sessions, models, effort levels) are supplied by the app and are a Reactor port note.",
      "props": {
        "label": "Model"
      },
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-root",
        "el": "button",
        "attrs": {
          "type": "button",
          "aria-haspopup": "listbox",
          "aria-label": "{label}"
        },
        "layout": {
          "mode": "horizontal",
          "gap": "1",
          "padding": {
            "left": "2",
            "right": "2"
          },
          "align": "center",
          "height": 32,
          "width": "hug"
        },
        "appearance": {
          "fontFamily": "body",
          "textStyle": "small",
          "color": "muted",
          "background": "$none",
          "radius": "sm"
        },
        "control": {
          "chrome": "none",
          "focus": { "kind": "outline", "color": "accent" }
        },
        "states": {
          "hover": { "background": "subtleHover" },
          "pressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "hoverPressed": { "background": "subtlePressed" },
          "disabled": { "color": "muted", "background": "$none" }
        },
        "on": { "click": { "open": "ComposerPickerOptions" } },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-label",
            "el": "span",
            "children": [
              "{label}"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-picker-chevron",
            "el": "svg",
            "attrs": {
              "width": "12",
              "height": "12",
              "viewBox": "0 0 24 24",
              "fill": "none",
              "aria-hidden": "true",
              "stroke": "currentColor",
              "stroke-width": "2",
              "stroke-linecap": "round",
              "stroke-linejoin": "round"
            },
            "appearance": {
              "color": "muted"
            },
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "composer-picker-chevron-path",
                "el": "path",
                "attrs": {
                  "d": "M6 9l6 6 6-6"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ComposerPickerOptions",
      "note": "Representative single-select flyout for the subtle composer pickers (model, session, reasoning-effort). Ships as a WinUI Flyout of RadioMenuItem rows on a `surface` (CardBackgroundFillColorDefault) sheet with 12px (`lg`) overlay corners (ChatPickerFlyoutStyle, #1459) and `md` shadow. Each row reserves a leading glyph column; the selected row shows an `accent` Segoe Fluent Icons CheckMark (glyph U+E73E, WinUI SymbolThemeFontFamily selection glyph, not a radio dot) while unselected rows keep the column empty so labels stay aligned. The check glyph carries a font-family-only raw style because the icon font is outside the display/body/mono token set (documented as the `icon` typography family in design.json); color stays token-bound to `accent`. Selecting a row closes the flyout; reopening restores defaults. Because `on.click.open` targets take no props, this shows a representative model list; the real model picker (AutoSuggestBox over a grouped ListView) and the effort slider/gauge are supplied by the app and are a Reactor port note.",
      "root": {
        "id": "composer-picker-options",
        "el": "div",
        "attrs": { "role": "menu", "aria-label": "Model" },
        "layout": { "mode": "vertical", "gap": "1", "padding": "1", "width": "hug" },
        "appearance": { "background": "surface", "color": "ink", "textStyle": "small", "radius": "lg", "shadow": "md" },
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "composer-option-sonnet",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "true" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
              { "id": "composer-option-sonnet-check", "el": "span", "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true", "style": "font-family:'Segoe Fluent Icons','Segoe MDL2 Assets',sans-serif" }, "layout": { "width": 16 }, "appearance": { "color": "accent", "textAlign": "center" }, "children": ["\uE73E"] },
              "Claude Sonnet 5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-option-opus",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "false" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
              { "id": "composer-option-opus-check", "el": "span", "attrs": { "aria-hidden": "true" }, "layout": { "width": 16 } },
              "Claude Opus 4.8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "composer-option-gpt",
            "el": "label",
            "attrs": { "role": "menuitemradio", "aria-checked": "false" },
            "layout": { "mode": "horizontal", "gap": "2", "align": "center", "padding": { "x": "2", "y": "1" } },
            "children": [
