              "GPT-5.6"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ChatBubble",
      "note": "Assistant chat turn: a 36×36 avatar (subtle `surface` fill, hairline `controlLine` border, `pill` radius) to the LEFT of plain prose that flows in the reading column with NO bubble, card, border, or fill (#1459). The refreshed assistant turn is bubbleless: only the user's own message rides a soft bubble (see ChatThread), so the transcript reads like a document rather than facing chat cards. Prose binds `ChatTextBrush` (`ink`) at body type (14/21 in-app); top-level blocks use one uniform 16px gap (token 3). Inline code and fenced code still get their own `ChatCardBrush` surfaces with `ChatSecondaryTextBrush` code text and a `bubble` (12px) radius, and the Copy action confirms with a `ChatCopySuccessBrush` checkmark that announces Copied and resets after two seconds. Footer reads timestamp · usage · Copy · Read aloud — Copy and Read aloud are hover-gated 20×20 subtle icon buttons in-app, and usage is the used/context (pct%) string ChatUsageFormatter produces. Mirrors ReactorChatTimeline's assistant row; ships via Reactor. Reading column max-width 768px, 16px prose inset, and the avatar hiding below 960px are Reactor port notes (no token equivalent). (This previews the assistant variant; the user variant rides the softer `ChatUserBrush` bubble on the right.)",
      "props": {
        "time": "2:14 PM",
        "usage": "12.5K/200K (6%)",
        "children": "Paired to the gateway — 6 Windows node capabilities are live."
