    {
      "name": "UserIdentityBadge",
      "note": "Owner / account identity from the Workspace PaneFooter (Windows/WorkspaceWindow.xaml #1541), and the sibling of AgentIdentityBadge: a 24px PersonPicture avatar to the LEFT of a two-line stack, the display name in body type over a connection-status line. Unlike AgentIdentityBadge, the status line pairs a small connection status dot with the caption `muted` label, dot on the LEFT of the status text. Reads the authenticated users.self profile (display name plus a live connection-status subtitle) with an honest Owner / Disconnected fallback; it never encodes authorization state. The dot follows connection state like the ConnectionStatusFlyout dots (`positive` connected, `warning` attention, `critical` error, `muted` unknown), never color alone. Ships as a subtle transparent WinUI Button that opens the Owner MenuFlyout: SubtleFillColorTransparent rest via `control.chrome:none`, `subtleHover`/`subtlePressed` through `states`, and a `control.focus` accent focus rectangle. In-app the avatar is a real PersonPicture (initials or account photo), previewed here with a person glyph.",
      "props": {
        "name": "Ada Lovelace",
        "status": "Connected"
      },
